  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 consistently outperforms scgpt by ~0.20 accuracy (0.725 vs 0.520) in the same multimodal/multiprofile/transformer/weighted setup, confirming the RNA encoder is the most impactful variable. However, PCA_n2000 (a linear, high-dimensional projection) has not been tested in the best configuration. This experiment (pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted + multiprofile) isolates the RNA encoder choice while holding all other parameters at their best-known values. It will clarify whether the learned non-linear scvi representation is essential or whether a simpler high-dim linear projection suffices. This is the best use of experiment 6 because the RNA encoder is the largest source of performance variance observed, and resolving this question with 4 experiments remaining will guide whether to exploit scvi-based configs or explore alternative RNA representations in the final budget."
